Oops...I should knew that package earlier. It's exactly the same as my proposal. For the Docker, I was able to reproduce the book Reproducible Research with R/RStudio from its source code on github <https://github.com/luckyrandom/Rep-Res-Book>. The book uses lots of packages and also absolute path, so it's not as easy as looks like. With the help of docker, I was able to get a clear prescription for reproducing the book. However, I'm not convinced on the usefulness of Docker for R developing, except for the special case. Most of R packages don't have any external dependencies, and packrat::restore should resolve the dependencies for most of R project.

Thanks!

Best,
Chenliang Xu

