Also make sure they give a bit of description when they apply to gsoc-r.
I've been swamped with applicants who say nothing about themselves and
often use alias names. I've found very few respond to requests for why
they are interested in R, and have been ignoring them for the last few
days as I'm in middle of house move. However, if there is a note with
the "application" e.g., I wish to mentor X on project Y, then I
immediately approve them.

JN

